by nicolas-grekas at 2026-10-25T07:56:39Z

#67408 changes `EncryptedTypes::register()`, and this PR removes that class.
After #67408, a type can be declared before its parent, and circular parents are rejected.
The type provider resolves parents lazily here, so the order doesn't matter.
But a cycle would only fail at runtime, as a circular service reference.
When rebasing, I'd keep a cycle check in `RegisterDoctrineDbalTypesPass`, so that the container reports it at compile time.

